{
  "title": "Sailing to Angel Island",
  "date": "2026-07-26",
  "intro": [
    "First time out sailing, from Marina Bay to Angel Island, on a calm, windless day."
  ],
  "location": "San Francisco Bay",
  "camera": "Canon EOS 350D",
  "cover": "IMG_9452.webp",
  "outro": [
    "My friend R went to Greece during the Summer for a couple of weeks to learn how to sail. On returning to SF he made some ",
    "sailing friends; he invited us to join him and his crew on a trip from Richmond to Angel Island. Besides the channel exiting Marina Bay, ",
    "it was practically windless most the way.",
    " We learnt that sailing folks like to complicate names for the sake of sounding special - starbird for the right side, port for the left. And no, it's not a map — it's a _chart_."
  ],

